# Memo derived metadata (lists/previews) — trace report

## Schema: what is stored

Derived content metadata lives in `MemoPayload.property` (store) and is exposed as `Memo.property` (API). Both proto definitions list the same five fields:

| Field | Type | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `has_link` | `bool` | Content contains a markdown link node |
| `has_task_list` | `bool` | Content contains a GFM task checkbox |
| `has_code` | `bool` | Content contains code (block, fenced block, or inline span) |
| `has_incomplete_tasks` | `bool` | At least one unchecked task checkbox |
| `title` | `string` | Plain text of the **first block-level H1** in the document |

```14:22:proto/store/memo.proto
  // The calculated properties from the memo content.
  message Property {
    bool has_link = 1;
    bool has_task_list = 2;
    bool has_code = 3;
    bool has_incomplete_tasks = 4;
    // The title extracted from the first H1 heading, if present.
    string title = 5;
  }
```

```271:279:proto/api/v1/memo_service.proto
  // Computed properties of a memo.
  message Property {
    bool has_link = 1;
    bool has_task_list = 2;
    bool has_code = 3;
    bool has_incomplete_tasks = 4;
    // The title extracted from the first H1 heading, if present.
    string title = 5;
  }
```

**Related but separate:** `tags` are recomputed in the same pass and stored in `MemoPayload.tags` (not inside `Property`). `snippet` is **not** derived metadata in payload — it is computed on read from raw `content` (see below).

---

## Computation site

### 1. Parser setup (`internal/markdown/markdown.go`)

Production `MarkdownService` is created with GFM + tag + mention extensions:

```47:61:server/router/api/v1/v1.go
func NewAPIV1Service(secret string, profile *profile.Profile, store *store.Store) *APIV1Service {
	markdownService := markdown.NewService(
		markdown.WithTagExtension(),
		markdown.WithMentionExtension(),
	)
	return &APIV1Service{
		// ...
		MarkdownService:          markdownService,
```

Parser construction:

```84:112:internal/markdown/markdown.go
func NewService(opts ...Option) Service {
	// ...
	exts := []goldmark.Extender{
		extension.GFM, // GitHub Flavored Markdown (tables, strikethrough, task lists, autolinks)
	}
	if cfg.enableTags {
		exts = append(exts, extensions.TagExtension)
	}
	if cfg.enableMentions {
		exts = append(exts, extensions.MentionExtension)
	}
	md := goldmark.New(
		goldmark.WithExtensions(exts...),
		goldmark.WithParserOptions(
			parser.WithAutoHeadingID(),
		),
	)
	return &service{ md: md }
}
```

`parse()` returns the goldmark AST document root:

```115:119:internal/markdown/markdown.go
func (s *service) parse(content []byte) (gast.Node, error) {
	reader := text.NewReader(content)
	doc := s.md.Parser().Parse(reader)
	return doc, nil
}
```

### 2. Core extraction — `ExtractAll` (`internal/markdown/markdown.go:355–422`)

Single AST walk populates `ExtractedData`:

```20:25:internal/markdown/markdown.go
type ExtractedData struct {
	Tags     []string
	Mentions []string
	Property *storepb.MemoPayload_Property
}
```

Property rules during the walk:

```383:408:internal/markdown/markdown.go
		// Check if the first block-level child of the document is an H1 heading.
		if !firstBlockChecked && n.Parent() != nil && n.Parent().Kind() == gast.KindDocument {
			firstBlockChecked = true
			if heading, ok := n.(*gast.Heading); ok && heading.Level == 1 {
				data.Property.Title = extractHeadingText(n, content)
			}
		}

		switch n.Kind() {
		case gast.KindLink:
			data.Property.HasLink = true
		case gast.KindCodeBlock, gast.KindFencedCodeBlock, gast.KindCodeSpan:
			data.Property.HasCode = true
		case east.KindTaskCheckBox:
			data.Property.HasTaskList = true
			if checkBox, ok := n.(*east.TaskCheckBox); ok {
				if !checkBox.IsChecked {
					data.Property.HasIncompleteTasks = true
				}
			}
```

Title extraction details (tests confirm):
- H1 must be the **first block-level child** of the document (`# Title` → `"Title"`)
- H2 first, or H1 after other text → `title = ""`
- Inline formatting stripped to plain text

`ExtractProperties` (`:192–241`) duplicates the same property logic in a standalone function; **production payload rebuild uses `ExtractAll`**, not `ExtractProperties`.

**Parser result → fields mapping:**

| AST node kind | Property field |
|---|---|
| First doc child `Heading` level 1 | `title` |
| `gast.KindLink` | `has_link` |
| `CodeBlock` / `FencedCodeBlock` / `CodeSpan` | `has_code` |
| `east.KindTaskCheckBox` | `has_task_list`; `has_incomplete_tasks` if unchecked |

Note: only `KindLink` is checked — GFM plain-URL autolinks (`KindAutoLink`) do **not** set `has_link` (only `[text](url)`-style links do; see test at `internal/markdown/markdown_test.go:352–363`).

### 3. Payload assembly — `RebuildMemoPayload` (`server/runner/memopayload/runner.go:74–88`)

```74:88:server/runner/memopayload/runner.go
func RebuildMemoPayload(_ context.Context, memo *store.Memo, markdownService markdown.Service) error {
	if memo.Payload == nil {
		memo.Payload = &storepb.MemoPayload{}
	}
	data, err := markdownService.ExtractAll([]byte(memo.Content))
	if err != nil {
		return errors.Wrap(err, "failed to extract markdown metadata")
	}
	memo.Payload.Tags = data.Tags
	memo.Payload.Property = data.Property
	return nil
}
```

`data.Mentions` is parsed but **not persisted** to payload in this function.

### 4. Persistence

`memo.payload` JSON column via `protojson.Marshal` on create/update (`store/db/sqlite/memo.go:19–26`, and analogous paths in mysql/postgres).

---

## Production operations that trigger recomputation

Only **`memopayload.RebuildMemoPayload`** writes derived `property` (and `tags`) to the DB.

| Operation | Trigger | Path |
|---|---|---|
| **CreateMemo** | Always, before `Store.CreateMemo` | `server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go:108` |
| **CreateMemoComment** | Indirectly — calls `CreateMemo` internally | `server/router/api/v1/memo_service_comments.go:56` → `memo_service.go:108` |
| **UpdateMemo** | Only when `update_mask` contains `"content"` | `server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go:436–451` |

```108:110:server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go
	if err := memopayload.RebuildMemoPayload(ctx, create, s.MarkdownService); err != nil {
		return nil, status.Errorf(codes.Internal, "failed to rebuild memo payload: %v", err)
	}
```

```436:451:server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go
		if path == "content" {
			// ...
			memo.Content = request.Memo.Content
			if err := memopayload.RebuildMemoPayload(ctx, memo, s.MarkdownService); err != nil {
				return nil, status.Errorf(codes.Internal, "failed to rebuild memo payload: %v", err)
			}
			update.Content = &memo.Content
			update.Payload = memo.Payload
```

**Does NOT recompute property:**
- `UpdateMemo` paths: `visibility`, `pinned`, `state`, timestamps, `location`, `attachments`, `relations` (`memo_service.go:452–493`)
- `ListMemos` / `GetMemo` — reads stored payload
- `DeleteMemo`, attachment/relation setters, reactions, shares

**Batch runner (not wired in production server):**

`memopayload.Runner.RunOnce` (`server/runner/memopayload/runner.go:27–72`) rebuilds all memos in batches, but `server/server.go:153–174` only starts the S3 presign runner — **`memopayload` is never registered or called at startup**.

**Secondary parse (mentions only, no payload write):**

`resolveMentionTargets` calls `ExtractAll` again on content for inbox notifications (`server/router/api/v1/memo_mention_helpers.go:32–35`), triggered after content updates via `dispatchMemoMentionNotificationsBestEffort` (`memo_service.go:510–511`). This does not update `property`.

---

## Call chain: write path

```
CreateMemo / UpdateMemo(content)
  → memopayload.RebuildMemoPayload                    [runner.go:74]
    → markdown.Service.ExtractAll(content)          [markdown.go:355]
      → service.parse(content)                        [markdown.go:116]
        → goldmark.Parser().Parse(reader)             [markdown.go:118]
      → gast.Walk(AST) → ExtractedData.Property       [markdown.go:371–411]
    → memo.Payload.Property = data.Property           [runner.go:86]
    → memo.Payload.Tags = data.Tags                   [runner.go:85]
  → store.CreateMemo / store.UpdateMemo               [memo_service.go:115 / :496]
    → protojson.Marshal(payload) → DB `memo.payload`
```

## Call chain: read path (lists/previews)

```
ListMemos / GetMemo
  → store.ListMemos / GetMemo  (payload JSON unmarshaled)
  → convertMemoFromStoreWithCreators                  [memo_service_converter.go:31]
    → memoMessage.Property = convertMemoPropertyFromStore(memo.Payload.Property)  [:47–50, :315–326]
    → memoMessage.Snippet = getMemoContentSnippet(memo.Content)                  [:76–80]
      → MarkdownService.GenerateSnippet(content, 64)   [memo_service_webhooks.go:83–89]
```

Property is **read from DB**; snippet is **recomputed from content** on every API response.

---

## How lists/previews consume derived metadata

### List filtering (server + client)

CEL filter schema maps boolean property fields to `memo.payload` JSON paths:

```186:228:internal/filter/schema.go
		"has_task_list": {
			JSONPath: []string{"property", "hasTaskList"},
		},
		"has_link": {
			JSONPath: []string{"property", "hasLink"},
		},
		"has_code": {
			JSONPath: []string{"property", "hasCode"},
		},
		"has_incomplete_tasks": {
			JSONPath: []string{"property", "hasIncompleteTasks"},
		},
```

Frontend maps UI filter factors → CEL:

```73:78:web/src/hooks/useMemoFilters.ts
      } else if (filter.factor === "property.hasLink") {
        conditions.push(`has_link`);
      } else if (filter.factor === "property.hasTaskList") {
        conditions.push(`has_task_list`);
      } else if (filter.factor === "property.hasCode") {
        conditions.push(`has_code`);
```

(`has_incomplete_tasks` is filterable server-side but has no UI filter chip.)

### Previews / list cards

- **`snippet`** (plain-text preview in relations, comments, API): generated at read time via `GenerateSnippet`, max 64 chars — not from `property`.
- **`property.title`**: stored and returned on `Memo.property.title`, but **no frontend consumer** was found; list/preview UIs render `content` or `snippet` directly.
- **RSS** uses its own `generateItemTitle` from the first line of raw content (`server/router/rss/rss.go:242–243, :302+`), not `property.title`.

### API field wiring

```47:51:server/router/api/v1/memo_service_converter.go
	if memo.Payload != nil {
		memoMessage.Tags = memo.Payload.Tags
		memoMessage.Property = convertMemoPropertyFromStore(memo.Payload.Property)
		memoMessage.Location = convertLocationFromStore(memo.Payload.Location)
	}
```

```315:326:server/router/api/v1/memo_service_converter.go
func convertMemoPropertyFromStore(property *storepb.MemoPayload_Property) *v1pb.Memo_Property {
	if property == nil {
		return nil
	}
	return &v1pb.Memo_Property{
		HasLink:            property.HasLink,
		HasTaskList:        property.HasTaskList,
		HasCode:            property.HasCode,
		HasIncompleteTasks: property.HasIncompleteTasks,
		Title:              property.Title,
	}
}
```

---

## Summary

| Question | Answer |
|---|---|
| **Computation site** | `internal/markdown/markdown.go` (`ExtractAll`), orchestrated by `server/runner/memopayload/runner.go` (`RebuildMemoPayload`) |
| **Parser** | goldmark + GFM + `TagExtension` + `MentionExtension`; AST walk via `gast.Walk` |
| **Production triggers** | `CreateMemo` (incl. comments), `UpdateMemo` when `content` in update mask |
| **Exact properties** | `has_link`, `has_task_list`, `has_code`, `has_incomplete_tasks`, `title` (+ co-recomputed `tags`) |
| **Lists** | Filter predicates read persisted `payload.property.*`; no re-parse |
| **Previews** | Use `snippet` (on-the-fly `GenerateSnippet`), not `property`; `property.title` is stored but unused in web UI |

